<p class="salutation">${greetingLine}</p>`;

let oldDriveFileId = dbRow.cl_drive_file_id || '';
if (!oldDriveFileId && sheetRow['Cover Letter']) {
  const match = String(sheetRow['Cover Letter']).match(/[-\w]{25,}/);
  if (match) oldDriveFileId = match[0];
}

const applicableRulesText = activeRules.length > 0
  ? activeRules.map((r, i) => `${i + 1}. ${r}`).join('\n')
  : '1. Keep the cover letter strictly to 1 page (260-320 words total across 5 paragraphs) in short, simple, human-like sentences (12-18 words per sentence). Never say "your team" (refer to the company by name).';

return [{
  json: {
    sNo,
    resumeId,
    company,
    cleanCompany,
    positionTitle,
    jobDescription,
    reviewerNotes,
    isForThisClOnly,
    hasReviewerNotes: reviewerNotes.length > 2,
    applicableRulesText,
    nextRevision,
    oldDriveFileId,
    salutationHtml: defaultSalutation,
    para1_hook_html: dbRow.para1_hook_html || `<p>I am writing to apply for the ${positionTitle} role at ${company}. What stood out to me in the job description is the focus on turning messy day-to-day operations into clean data models and reliable reports. Before spending the last five years in data analytics, I ran my own small marketing agency for ten years. That mix taught me how much time teams lose when numbers do not match across different tools. Fixing those gaps between business teams and engineering is the part of the job I enjoy most.</p>`,
    para2_stewardship_html: dbRow.para2_stewardship_html || `<p>Outside of writing SQL queries and building Tableau dashboards, I spend my free time on my terrace in Gurugram growing mushrooms and automating small daily tasks with n8n. Growing mushrooms in North India's weather is not a fancy hobby. It comes down to watching basic details closely. If moisture or airflow slips even a little, the whole batch fails. I bring that same habit to my work when I check data quality, map workflows, or build reports that leaders rely on.</p>`,
    para3_impact_story_html: dbRow.para3_impact_story_html || `<p>I also believe analysis is only useful when it solves a real problem on the ground. At Concentrix, our hiring data showed that new joiners were struggling once they started work. Sending another dashboard to management was not fixing the issue. I looked closely at the hiring steps and worked with leadership to bring our training team directly into the interview stage. That simple change improved hire quality by 84%. In my current role at Highspring India, I use the same practical approach across four engineering teams to automate recurring reports and cut manual work by 40%.</p>`,
    para4_resilience_html: dbRow.para4_resilience_html || `<p>My day-to-day work covers SQL, Python, Tableau, and working closely with business and tech teams. If the team at ${company} uses an internal tool I have not worked with yet, I learn new systems quickly. Practical challenges early in my career taught me how to stay resourceful, focus on the basics, and get things done without hand-holding. When I take ownership of a task, nobody has to follow up twice.</p>`,
    para5_closing_html: dbRow.para5_closing_html || `<p>I would welcome the chance to bring this steady, practical approach to ${company}. Thank you for your time and consideration, and I look forward to speaking with you soon.</p>`,
    _activeModel: 'gemini-3.5-flash-lite'
  }
}];

parameters.jsonBody:
={{ JSON.stringify({
  contents: [{
    parts: [{
      text: `You are the Self-Learning Cover Letter Editor for Sumanto Banerjee.

Target Role: ${$json.positionTitle} at ${$json.company}
Contains 'For this cover letter / resume' One-Off Flag: ${$json.isForThisClOnly}
